      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-108932",
      ":question/problem": "Three journalists ask people on the street for interviews.\nOf the people asked, $20%$ of them accept the interview, independently of which journalist asks. If the three journalists ask $10$, $5$, and $15$ people, respectively, for an interview, what is the probability that at least $2$ people will accept the interview?\nRound your answer to $4$ decimal places."
