      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-109475",
      ":question/problem": "A company manufacturers bolts using two machines, machine $A$ and machine $B$. The probability that either machine will produce a defective bolt is $6%$. If machine $A$ produces $6$ bolts per minute, and machine $B$ produces $8$ bolts per minute, what is the probability that among the bolts produced by both machines in a given minute, there will be at least $3$ defective bolts? Round your answer to $4$ decimal places. You may assume that machines $A$ and $B$ produce bolts independently."
